.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt AKTURE-GREETER 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm akture-greeter
.Nd login screen of the akture display manager
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
draws the login screen of
.Xr akture 8 .
It is started by
.Xr akture 8
as the unprivileged user
.Dq _akture
with its end of a socketpair on descriptor 3, and is not meant to be
run by hand.
It reads no configuration itself: the options meant for it, the
sessions and the last user arrive from the master.
.Pp
The screen is drawn into a shared memory image with
.Xr pixman 3
and FreeType, and sent with MIT-SHM; no drawing requests or extensions
of the X server are used otherwise.
Only the parts that changed are drawn and sent, so the greeter uses no
CPU while nothing happens apart from updating the clock once a minute.
Backgrounds are mapped from
.Pa .akbg
files without conversion.
The keyboard is grabbed for the whole time the screen is shown.
.Ss Keys
.Bl -tag -width "BackSpace" -compact
.It Tab
move to the next control (Shift+Tab: previous)
.It Enter
log in, or activate the selected control
.It BackSpace
delete the last character
.It Ctrl+U
clear the field
.It Esc
clear the field and return to the last user
.El
.Pp
The controls are the field, the session menu, the switch to another
user, the keyboard layout and, if allowed, the power menu.
Characters typed while another control is selected go to the field.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr akture-conv 1 ,
.Xr akture.conf 5 ,
.Xr akture 8
